Renderer execution contract
Public filtering scriptlets may run in the matching document's main world.
Several required scripts replace page globals (fetch, XMLHttpRequest and
property values); password-world execution would not implement their effects.
Four required scriptlets declare ISOLATED in upstream metadata; the lock retains
that distinction even though adblock-rust returns one combined injected_script.
The approved combined-output route uses main world without credentials,
secrets, privileged bindings or native password access. It must never reuse
Boaz's trusted password script channel. Injection timing and document identity,
site exceptions, procedural cosmetics and renderer lifecycle remain runtime
acceptance gates. These files establish source provenance, not product parity.
